# =============================================================================
# ISC BIND / named Query Log — Format Documentation
# =============================================================================
# Auto-detected when ALL THREE keywords appear in the first 600 bytes:
#   "named"   "query:"   " IN "
#
# No CSV header row — each line is parsed by regex.
# Lines beginning with '#' are treated as comments and ignored.
#
# Required line pattern (regex):
#   <timestamp> ... named[<pid>]: ... query: <domain> IN <TYPE> ...
#
# Standard field  ←  Extracted from
# --------------  -----------------------------------------------------------
# timestamp       ← syslog-style prefix  (e.g. "Jan 15 08:00:00")
#                   OR named-style prefix (e.g. "15-Jan-2024 08:00:00.123")
# domain          ← FQDN before " IN "   (trailing dot stripped)
# query_type      ← record type after " IN "  (A, AAAA, TXT, MX, …)
# query_length    ← computed from len(domain)
# subdomain_count ← computed from label count
# response_size   ← defaults to 0 (not present in query-only logs)
#
# Example line:
#   Jan 15 08:00:00 ns1 named[5678]: client 10.0.0.1#5432 (example.com):
#       query: example.com IN A + (8.8.8.8)
# =============================================================================
Jan 15 08:00:00 ns1 named[5678]: client 192.168.1.0#5432 (google.com): query: google.com IN A + (8.8.8.8)
Jan 15 08:00:10 ns1 named[5678]: client 192.168.1.1#5432 (a8f3kq2.tunnel.example.com): query: a8f3kq2.tunnel.example.com IN TXT + (8.8.8.8)
Jan 15 08:00:20 ns1 named[5678]: client 192.168.1.2#5432 (github.com): query: github.com IN AAAA + (8.8.8.8)
